  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every refusal added by this task. Fail closed with a stable `reasonCode` (the `sdap.provision.*` / `sdap.unsecure.*` convention at `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:141-156`). An unreadable membership count, an unreadable BU-user count, a missing team, a second matching team, or a team with any member REFUSES — never falls back to the default team, the root BU or the caller's BU.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: named-team resolution. Resolve by (Secure Record BU id AND team name from configuration AND `teamtype eq 0` AND `isdefault eq false`), `$top=2`, exactly one match required. Configuration key `SecureRecord:OwnerTeamName` sits beside `SecureRecord:BusinessUnitName` with a compiled default, mirroring `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:94-133` — a name, never a GUID.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the memberless invariant. "Zero members" means zero `teammembership` rows of ANY principal kind (human or application user). "No-user BU" means zero systemusers — enabled or disabled, human or application — whose `businessunitid` is the Secure Record BU. Both are checked at provisioning time before any mutation, and both are clauses of the standing assertion.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: generalized provisioning/unsecure. Extend the EXISTING endpoints and DTOs to accept `RecordType` (sprk_project | sprk_matter | sprk_workassignment) + `RecordId`, keeping the legacy `ProjectId` field and routes working for the shipped wizard. Do NOT add parallel per-entity endpoints (CLAUDE.md §11). The delegation filter resolves the SAME root the handler uses (the `FromGrantRoot` pattern at `DelegationRuleFilter.cs:216-229`) — the record authorized is the record re-owned.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: matters and work assignments. A secure matter/work assignment gets exactly what a secure project gets: named-team ownership verified by read-back, creator share (task 061 semantics), its own SPE container recorded on its own `sprk_containerid`. A secure root that cannot receive its own container is refused, not half-provisioned — otherwise uploads 409 forever (`RecordContainerResolver.cs:244-266`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: migration. Dry run is the default and prints the full plan; `-Apply` is required to write. Idempotent (a second run changes nothing). Every reassignment is verified by read-back. Existing POA shares on migrated rows are preserved and counted before and after. Auth is an explicit-URL `az` token as in the setup guide §2 — never `pac`'s active profile, and never a new client secret (ADR-028 A4).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the org setting `organization.sharetopreviousowneronassign`. If it is true, every assign in this task shares the record back to the PREVIOUS owner — for the migration that is the default team, i.e. every future user placed in the BU. Read it before the first assign; if true, STOP (escalation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: all enforcement. No Dataverse plugin. Runtime enforcement lives in the BFF provisioning path; standing enforcement is the NFR-05 live assertion run as a MANUAL gate (no Dataverse in CI — owner 2026-09-10). Do not propose relocating test users.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: this task's deliverable. It delivers a 100% fix of C10 part 1 for all three entity types; discovered scope is added here, not deferred. A document-only save with no related record stays a supported path — nothing here may make a target record required.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; measure publish size against a FRESH master build from a short path with the same zip tool, report both absolute sizes, the delta and the file counts; ceiling 60 MB; run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed here. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests. Use the existing `ProvisionProjectTestFixture` roster fakes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

